12:07:22 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ["American Broadcasting Company\nWhat talk shows and soap operas are on ABC's daytime schedule?", 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 1: Currently, ABC\'s daytime schedule features talk shows "The View" and "The Chew," along with the soap opera "General Hospital."', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 2: How long has "General Hospital" been on the ABC daytime schedule?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 2: "General Hospital" has been on the ABC daytime schedule since 1963, making it the longest-running entertainment program in the history of the ABC television network.', "American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 3: What was ABC's daytime schedule before 1975?", 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 3: ABC\'s daytime schedule before 1975 did not have the current lineup, but it has featured talk shows like "The View" and "The Chew," and the soap opera "General Hospital."', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 4: When was the soap opera All My Children on the ABC daytime schedule?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 4: The soap opera "All My Children" aired on the ABC daytime schedule from 1970 to 2011.', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 5: When was the soap opera One Life to Live on the ABC daytime schedule?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 5: The soap opera "One Life to Live" was on the ABC daytime schedule from 1968 until 2012.', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 6: What past soap operas were aired on ABC before 2011?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 6: Some past soap operas seen on the ABC daytime schedule before 2011 include "Ryan\'s Hope," "Dark Shadows," "Loving," "The City," and "Port Charles."', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 7: What happened to "The Edge of Night"?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 7: The soap opera "The Edge of Night" was cancelled by CBS in 1975, and its last nine years were aired on the ABC daytime schedule.', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 8: What game shows were aired on ABC daytime?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 8: ABC has also aired a number of game shows, including "The Dating Game," "The Newlywed Game," "Let\'s Make a Deal," "Password," "Split Second," "The $10,000/$20,000 Pyramid," "Family Feud," "The Better Sex," "Trivia Trap," "All-Star Blitz," and "Hot Streak."', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 9: What does the question "Is Good Morning America considered to be part of the ABC Daytime block?" imply?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nAnswer 9: The question "Is Good Morning America considered to be part of the ABC Daytime block?" is implying that Good Morning America is broadcast during the same time period as the daytime programming on ABC.', "American Broadcasting Company\nABC's daytime schedule currently features talk shows The View and The Chew, and the soap opera General Hospital, the latter of which is the longest-running entertainment program in the history of the ABC television network, having aired since 1963. ABC also broadcasts the morning news program Good Morning America and has done so since 1975, though that program is not considered to be part of the ABC Daytime block. In addition to the long-running All My Children (1970–2011) and One Life to Live (1968–2012), notable past soap operas seen on the daytime lineup include Ryan's Hope, Dark Shadows, Loving, The City and Port Charles. ABC also aired the last nine years of the Procter & Gamble-produced soap The Edge of Night, following its cancellation by CBS in 1975. ABC Daytime has also aired a number of game shows, including The Dating Game, The Newlywed Game, Let's Make a Deal, Password, Split Second, The $10,000/$20,000 Pyramid, Family Feud, The Better Sex, Trivia Trap, All-Star Blitz and Hot Streak."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': "ABC's daytime schedule currently features talk shows The View and The Chew, and the soap oper