12:13:52 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Southern California\nWhat is Southern California?', 'Southern California\nAnswer 1: Southern California consists of a diverse collection of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem landscapes in the state and country.', 'Southern California\nQuestion 2: What are some of the landscapes included in Southern California?', 'Southern California\nAnswer 2: Some of the landscapes included in Southern California are Pacific Ocean islands, shorelines, beaches, coastal plains, the Transverse and Peninsular Ranges, peaks, interior valleys, and vast deserts.', 'Southern California\nQuestion 3: How do the landscapes of Southern California compare to other regions in the state and country?', 'Southern California\nAnswer 3: Southern California has one of the more varied collections of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem landscapes than other major regions in the state and country.', 'Southern California\nWrite the following sentences in the question-answer format.', 'Southern California\nPassage:Some four hundred million years ago, an ancient inland sea flooded part of the continent that was to become Texas. Deep layers of sandstone, limestone, and dolomite were deposited by waves and currents. River, swamp and lake sediments accumulated on the sea floor, and were topped by windblown sand. Over time, as the sea retreated, these strata were lifted up and folded, forming the geologic "plateau" on which the town of Marathon stands today. The alternating layers of dark shale, limestone, and sandstone that make up the plateau formed some of the classic landscapes of the Texas desert.', 'Southern California\nQuestion 4:  What happened 400 million years ago in the region that is now Texas?', 'Southern California\nAnswer 4: An ancient inland sea flooded part of the continent that was to become Texas.', 'Southern California\nQuestion 5: What types of deposits were formed by the sea and the land during this period?', 'Southern California\nAnswer 5: Deep layers of sandstone, limestone, and dolomite were deposited by waves and currents. River, swamp, and lake sediments accumulated on the sea floor, and windblown sand formed on top.', 'Southern California\nQuestion 6: What happened to these layers of sediment as time went on?', 'Southern California\nAnswer 6: As the sea retreated, these strata were lifted up and folded, forming the geologic "plateau" on which the town of Marathon stands today.', 'Southern California\nQuestion 7: What are some of the classic landscapes found on this plateau?', 'Southern California\nAnswer 7: Some of the classic landscapes found on this plateau are alternating layers of dark shale, limestone, and sandstone.', 'Southern California\nIs there any other information you would like me to include? This summary does not provide any additional information.', 'Southern California\nSouthern California consists of one of the more varied collections of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem landscapes in a diversity outnumbering other major regions in the state and country. The region spans from Pacific Ocean islands, shorelines, beaches, and coastal plains, through the Transverse and Peninsular Ranges with their peaks, into the large and small interior valleys, to the vast deserts of California.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Southern California', 'context': 'Southern California consists of one of the more varied collections of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem landscapes in a diversity outnumbering other major regions in the state and country. The region spans from Pacific Ocean islands, shorelines, beaches, and coastal plains, through the Transverse and Peninsular Ranges with their peaks, into the large and small interior valleys, to the vast deserts of California.', 'question': 'Topic: Southern California\nThe region spans starting at islands found in which body of water?', 'answer': 'Pacific Ocean'}, {'title': 'Southern California', 'context': 'Southern California consists of one of the more varied collections of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem landscapes in a diversity outnumbering other major regions in the state and country. The region spans from Pacific Ocean islands, shorelines, beaches, and coastal plains, through the Transverse and Peninsular Ranges with their peaks, into the large and small interior valleys, to the vast deserts of California.', 'question': "Topic: Southern California\nWhat term best describes southern California's collection of landscapes?", 'answer': 'varied'}, {'title': 'Southern California', 'context': 'Southern California consists of one of the more varied collections of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem landscapes in a diversity outnumbering other major regions in the state and country. The region spans from Pacific Ocean islands, shorelines, beaches, and coastal plains, through the Transverse and Peninsular Ranges with their peaks, into the large and small interior valleys, to the vast deserts of California.', 'question': 'Topic: Southern California\nWhat type of landscapes other than geologic and natural ecosystem landscapes can be found in southern California?', 'answer': 'topographic'}, {'title': 'Southern California', 'context': 'Southern California consists of one of the more varied collections of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem landscapes in a diversity outnumbering other major regions in the state and country. The region spans from Pacific Ocean islands, shorelines, beaches, and coastal plains, through the Transverse and Peninsular Ranges with their peaks, into the large and small interior valleys, to the vast deserts of California.', 'question': 'Topic: Southern California\nThe region spans which mountains other than the Transverse ranges?', 'answer': 'Peninsular'}, {'title': 'Southern California', 'context': 'Southern California consists of one of the more varied collections of geologic, topographic, and natural ecosystem 