 Science Center at the Fresno MetroDome, and the Fresno Philharmonic. Other popular attractions include the Fresno Art Museum and the historic downtown area.', 'Fresno, California\nQuestion 3:  Are there any notable landmarks in Fresno City?', 'Fresno, California\nAnswer 3:  Yes, there are several notable landmarks in Fresno City. These include the Armenian Genocide Memorial, the Chinese Temple and Gardens, and the Korean Cultural Center, which hosts a variety of cultural events throughout the year.', 'Fresno, California\nQuestion 4:  What are some popular outdoor activities in Fresno City?', "Fresno, California\nAnswer 4:  There are many outdoor activities to enjoy in Fresno City. Hiking and biking are popular in the city's parks, including the Gray Lodge State Recreation Area and the Yosemite Conservation Heritage, which includes the American River Parkway and the Kings River Recreation Area. Additionally, visitors can enjoy fishing, hunting, and camping in nearby state parks and wildlife areas.", 'Fresno, California\nThe neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhere is the neighborhood of Sunnyside located in Fresno?', 'answer': "Fresno's far southeast side"}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhat are the two major thoroughfares of Sunnyside?', 'answer': 'Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhen was most of Sunnside developed?', 'answer': '1950s through the 1970s'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhere is the home of the Sunnyside Country Club?', 'answer': 'Sunnyside'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWho designed the golf course located at the Sunnyside Country Club?', 'answer': 'William P. Bell'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
