12:44:47 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ["American Broadcasting Company\nWhat was launched in ABC's seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968?", 'American Broadcasting Company\nLOVE Radio, a new programming concept spearheaded by Allen Shaw and developed by ABC Radio to compete with progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations.', 'American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 2: What was the primary goal of launching LOVE Radio?', 'American Broadcasting Company\nThe primary goal was to provide a limited selection of music genres for the stations, which could compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations.', "American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 3: How did ABC Radio's FM affiliates react to the LOVE Radio concept?", 'American Broadcasting Company\nNot all affiliates adopted the LOVE Radio concept, with some (like KXYZ) retaining their majority content.', "American Broadcasting Company\nQuestion 4: When was Shaw's announcement to review ABC FM's music choice policy made, and what was the reason for the review?", 'American Broadcasting Company\nThe review was announced in August 1970, to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'American Broadcasting Company\nYou are an AI assistant that follows instruction extremely well. Help as much as you can.', 'American Broadcasting Company\nIn July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': "Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nWho lead the 1968 special programming for ABC Radio's FM stations?", 'answer': 'Allen Shaw'}, {'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': 'Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nWho was the ABC Radio president in 1968?', 'answer': 'Harold L. Neal'}, {'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': 'Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nWhat was the name for the new radio concept designed by Allen Shaw?', 'answer': 'LOVE Radio'}, {'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': 'Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nHow many ABC music stations were owned-and-operated in 1968?', 'answer': 'seven'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
