13:06:48 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Oxygen\nHow is oxygen stored?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 1:  Oxygen storage methods include high pressure oxygen tanks, cryogenics and chemical compounds.', 'Oxygen\nQuestion 2:  What is one liter of liquid oxygen equivalent to?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 2:  One liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F).', 'Oxygen\nQuestion 3:  How is oxygen transported in bulk?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 3:  Oxygen is often transported in bulk as a liquid in specially insulated tankers.', 'Oxygen\nQuestion 4:  Why is oxygen transported in special insulated tankers?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 4:  Oxygen is transported in special insulated tankers because one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F), which makes it a more economical method of transport.', 'Oxygen\nQuestion 5:  Where is oxygen stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas useful?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 5:  Oxygen is stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas that is useful in certain portable medical applications and oxy-fuel welding and cutting.', 'Oxygen\nQuestion 6:  What is liquid oxygen converted to before it enters a building?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 6:  Liquid oxygen is passed through heat exchangers, which convert the cryogenic liquid into gas before it enters the building.', 'Oxygen\nQuestion 7:  Where do bulk liquid oxygen storage containers stand?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 7:  Bulk liquid oxygen storage containers stand outside hospitals and other institutions with a need for large volumes of pure oxygen gas.', 'Oxygen\nQuestion 8:  What are the benefits of transporting oxygen as a liquid?', 'Oxygen\nAnswer 8:  One benefit of transporting oxygen as a liquid is its compactness - one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F). Another benefit is that oxygen is a non-combustible fluid, which means it is relatively safe to transport.', 'Oxygen\nOxygen storage methods include high pressure oxygen tanks, cryogenics and chemical compounds. For reasons of economy, oxygen is often transported in bulk as a liquid in specially insulated tankers, since one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F). Such tankers are used to refill bulk liquid oxygen storage containers, which stand outside hospitals and other institutions with a need for large volumes of pure oxygen gas. Liquid oxygen is passed through heat exchangers, which convert the cryogenic liquid into gas before it enters the building. Oxygen is also stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas; a form that is useful in certain portable medical applications and oxy-fuel welding and cutting.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Oxygen', 'context': 'Oxygen storage methods include high pressure oxygen tanks, cryogenics and chemical compounds. For reasons of economy, oxygen is often transported in bulk as a liquid in specially insulated tankers, since one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F). Such tankers are used to refill bulk liquid oxygen storage containers, which stand outside hospitals and other institutions with a need for large volumes of pure oxygen gas. Liquid oxygen is passed through heat exchangers, which convert the cryogenic liquid into gas before it enters the building. Oxygen is also stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas; a form that is useful in certain portable medical applications and oxy-fuel welding and cutting.', 'question': 'Topic: Oxygen\nWhat do oxygen tanks, cryogenics, and chemical compounds serve as for oxygen?', 'answer': 'storage'}, {'title': 'Oxygen', 'context': 'Oxygen storage methods include high pressure oxygen tanks, cryogenics and chemical compounds. For reasons of economy, oxygen is often transported in bulk as a liquid in specially insulated tankers, since one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F). Such tankers are used to refill bulk liquid oxygen storage containers, which stand outside hospitals and other institutions with a need for large volumes of pure oxygen gas. Liquid oxygen is passed through heat exchangers, which convert the cryogenic liquid into gas before it enters the building. Oxygen is also stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas; a form that is useful in certain portable medical applications and oxy-fuel welding and cutting.', 'question': 'Topic: Oxygen\nBy what means is bulk oxygen shipped?', 'answer': 'insulated tankers'}, {'title': 'Oxygen', 'context': 'Oxygen storage methods include high pressure oxygen tanks, cryogenics and chemical compounds. For reasons of economy, oxygen is often transported in bulk as a liquid in specially insulated tankers, since one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F). Such tankers are used to refill bulk liquid oxygen storage containers, which stand outside hospitals and other institutions with a need for large volumes of pure oxygen gas. Liquid oxygen is passed through heat exchangers, which convert the cryogenic liquid into gas before it enters the building. Oxygen is also stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas; a form that is useful in certain portable medical applications and oxy-fuel welding and cutting.', 'question': 'Topic: Oxygen\nIn what state is oxygen shipped in bulk?', 'answer': 'liquid'}, {'title': 'Oxygen', 'context': 'Oxygen storage methods include high pressure oxygen tanks, cryogenics and chemical compounds. For reasons of economy, oxygen is often transported in bulk as a liquid in specially insulated tankers, since one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F). Such tankers are used to refill bulk liquid oxygen storage containers, which stand outside hospitals and other institutions with a need for large volumes of pure oxygen gas. Liquid oxygen is passed through heat exchangers, which convert the cryogenic liquid into gas before it enters the building. Oxygen is also stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas; a form that is useful in certain portable medical applications and oxy-fuel welding and cutting.', 'question': 'Topic: Oxygen\nIn what form is oxygen transported in smaller containers?', 'answer': 'compressed gas'}, {'title': 'Oxygen', 'context': 'Oxygen storage methods include high pressure oxygen tanks, cryogenics and chemical compounds. For reasons of economy, oxygen is often transported in bulk as a liquid in specially insulated tankers, since one liter of liquefied oxygen is equivalent to 840 liters of gaseous oxygen at atmospheric pressure and 20 °C (68 °F). Such tankers are used to refill bulk liquid oxygen storage containers, which stand outside hospitals and other institutions with a need for large volumes of pure oxygen gas. Liquid oxygen is passed through heat exchangers, which convert the cryogenic liquid into gas before it enters the building. Oxygen is also stored and shipped in smaller cylinders containing the compressed gas; a form that is useful in certain portable medical applications and oxy-fuel welding and cutting.', 'question': 'Topic: Oxygen\nWhat type of organization would need large quantities of pure oxygen?', 'answer': 'hospitals'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
