imates are accurate, the oil reserves in Turkana could have a significant impact on Kenya's economy. The country currently relies heavily on oil imports, so discovering its own reserves could help reduce its reliance on imports and save money on the national import bill. Additionally, the oil industry could create jobs and boost other industries such as transportation and manufacturing.", 'Kenya\nHowever, there are also potential challenges associated with oil extraction in Turkana. The region is still developing and may not have the infrastructure needed to support a large-scale oil industry. Additionally, there may be environmental concerns related to oil extraction in the area.', "Kenya\nOverall, the discovery of oil reserves in Turkana is an exciting development for Kenya's economy, but there are still many factors to consider before the true impact can be determined.", "Kenya\nKenya has proven deposits of oil in Turkana and the commercial viability was just discovered. Tullow Oil estimates Kenya's oil reserves to be around 10 billion barrels. Exploration is still continuing to determine if there are more reserves. Kenya currently imports all crude petroleum requirements. Kenya, east Africa's largest economy, has no strategic reserves and relies solely on oil marketers' 21-day oil reserves required under industry regulations. Petroleum accounts for 20% to 25% of the national import bill."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Kenya', 'context': "Kenya has proven deposits of oil in Turkana and the commercial viability was just discovered. Tullow Oil estimates Kenya's oil reserves to be around 10 billion barrels. Exploration is still continuing to determine if there are more reserves. Kenya currently imports all crude petroleum requirements. Kenya, east Africa's largest economy, has no strategic reserves and relies solely on oil marketers' 21-day oil reserves required under industry regulations. Petroleum accounts for 20% to 25% of the national import bill.", 'question': 'Topic: Kenya\nWhere does Kenya have deposits of oil?', 'answer': 'in Turkana'}, {'title': 'Kenya', 'context': "Kenya has proven deposits of oil in Turkana and the commercial viability was just discovered. Tullow Oil estimates Kenya's oil reserves to be around 10 billion barrels. Exploration is still continuing to determine if there are more reserves. Kenya currently imports all crude petroleum requirements. Kenya, east Africa's largest economy, has no strategic reserves and relies solely on oil marketers' 21-day oil reserves required under industry regulations. Petroleum accounts for 20% to 25% of the national import bill.", 'question': 'Topic: Kenya\nHow many barrels of oil is it estimated Kenya has?', 'answer': 'around 10 billion barrels.'}, {'title': 'Kenya', 'context': "Kenya has proven deposits of oil in Turkana and the commercial viability was just discovered. Tullow Oil estimates Kenya's oil reserves to be around 10 billion barrels. Exploration is still continuing to determine if there are more reserves. Kenya currently imports all crude petroleum requirements. Kenya, east Africa's largest economy, has no strategic reserves and relies solely on oil marketers' 21-day oil reserves required under industry regulations. Petroleum accounts for 20% to 25% of the national import bill.", 'question': 'Topic: Kenya\nWhat is Kenya doing to determine if there are more reserves?', 'answer': 'Exploration'}, {'title': 'Kenya', 'context': "Kenya has proven deposits of oil in Turkana and the commercial viability was just discovered. Tullow Oil estimates Kenya's oil reserves to be around 10 billion barrels. Exploration is still continuing to determine if there are more reserves. Kenya currently imports all crude petroleum requirements. Kenya, east Africa's largest economy, has no strategic reserves and relies solely on oil marketers' 21-day oil reserves required under industry regulations. Petroleum accounts for 20% to 25% of the national import bill.", 'question': 'Topic: K