hat require more specific details might need to be adjusted accordingly.', "Kenya\nLet's read the following passage and rewrite it in a question-answer format.", 'Kenya\nPassage:', "Kenya\nPeople talk a lot about some woman claiming to be the love of Michael Jackson's life, but more interesting is this list of the top 15 women for whom music's hungriest prince of the pop world's lust is written. This song reveals how much it hurts to be the one Michael wanted. The song's singer arrives on his doorstep, but he is nowhere to be found. All the lyrics are sad requests from this former love that he will listen and reply to her calls for his love. Michael was afraid the relationship was never a marriage proposal, even though they were seeing each other for so long.", 'Kenya\nQuestion 1: Who is the woman mentioned in the passage?', "Kenya\nAnswer 1: The woman mentioned in the passage is Michael Jackson's former love whose song he wrote.", "Kenya\nQuestion 2: How do the lyrics of the song express Michael Jackson's feelings?", "Kenya\nAnswer 2: The lyrics express Michael Jackson's feelings of sadness and pain, as he seems to be missing his former love and longing for their relationship to be a true marriage proposal.", 'Kenya\nQuestion 3: What is the situation described in the song?', "Kenya\nAnswer 3: The situation described in the song is a former love visiting Michael Jackson's doorstep, but he is nowhere to be found. This former love is asking for his attention and calling for his love, but he does not seem to be responsive.", 'Kenya\nQuestion 4: Why was Michael Jackson afraid that his relationship with the woman was not a marriage proposal?', 'Kenya\nAnswer 4: Michael Jackson was afraid that his relationship with the woman was not a marriage proposal because all the lyrics in the song are sad requests from this former love that he will listen and reply to her calls for his love, which suggests that she is still longing for their relationship to be a true marriage proposal, but Michael Jackson has moved on.', 'Kenya\nQuestion 5: What is the emotion being conveyed in this song?', 'Kenya\nAnswer 5: The emotion being conveyed in this song is sadness and longing, as it captures the pained feelings of a former love who is waiting for Michael Jackson to respond to her calls for his love, but he seems to be avoiding her.', "Kenya\nKenya (/ˈkɛnjə/; locally [ˈkɛɲa] ( listen)), officially the Republic of Kenya, is a country in Africa and a founding member of the East African Community (EAC). Its capital and largest city is Nairobi. Kenya's territory lies on the equator and overlies the East African Rift covering a diverse and expansive terrain that extends roughly from Lake Victoria to Lake Turkana (formerly called Lake Rudolf) and further south-east to the Indian Ocean. It is bordered by Tanzania to the south, Uganda to the west, South Sudan to the north-west, Ethiopia to the north and Somalia to the north-east. Kenya covers 581,309 km2 (224,445 sq mi), and had a population of approximately 45 million people in July 2014."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Kenya', 'context': "Kenya (/ˈkɛnjə/; locally [ˈkɛɲa] ( listen)), officially the Republic of Kenya, is a country in Africa and a founding member of the East African Community (EAC). Its capital and largest city is Nairobi. Kenya's territory lies on the equator and overlies the East African Rift covering a diverse and expansive terrain that extends roughly from Lake Victoria to Lake Turkana (formerly called Lake Rudolf) and further south-east to the Indian Ocean. It is bordered by Tanzania to the south, Uganda to the west, South Sudan to the north-west, Ethiopia to the north and Somalia to the north-east. Kenya covers 581,309 km2 (224,445 sq mi), and had a population of approximately 45 million people in July 2014.", 'question': 'Topic: Kenya\nWhere is Kenya located?', 'answer': 'in Africa'}, {'title': 'Kenya', 'context': "Kenya (/ˈkɛnjə/; locally [ˈkɛɲa] ( listen)), officially the Republic o