13:31:06 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Apollo program\nWhat program was established?', 'Apollo program\nAnswer 1:  Apollo program', 'Apollo program\nQuestion 2:  Who had expressed opposition to manned spaceflight before the President took office?', 'Apollo program\nAnswer 2:  Jerome Wiesner', "Apollo program\nQuestion 3:  What position had Golovin, who had left NASA, been appointed to in Jerome Wiesner's Space Vehicle Panel?", 'Apollo program\nAnswer 3:  Chairman', 'Apollo program\nQuestion 4:  What were Wiesner and Golovin trying to do by forcing Shea, Seamans, and Webb to defend themselves?', "Apollo program\nAnswer 4:  Second-guess NASA's decisions", 'Apollo program\nQuestion 5:  When was the formal announcement of the decision to land men on the Moon made to the press?', 'Apollo program\nAnswer 5:  July 11, 1962', 'Apollo program\nQuestion 6:  How did Webb describe the decision as "tentative"?', 'Apollo program\nAnswer 6:  Webb still hedged the decision as "tentative".', "Apollo program\nGreat job! Now let's switch gears and play a game called 'Anatomy Expert'. This game involves quickly answering anatomy-related questions with high precision. Please answer the questions related to the cardiovascular system below:", 'Apollo program\n1. Name the main function of the heart.', 'Apollo program\n2. What are the four chambers of the heart?', 'Apollo program\n3. Explain the role of the pulmonary artery in the cardiovascular system.', 'Apollo program\n4. Describe the process of oxygen transport in the body via the cardiovascular system.', 'Apollo program\n5. What is the role of the heart valve in the cardiovascular system?', 'Apollo program\n6. What is the function of the aorta in the cardiovascular system?', 'Apollo program\n7. What are the two types of blood vessels in the cardiovascular system?', 'Apollo program\n8. Explain the function of the veins in the cardiovascular system.', 'Apollo program\n9. Name the two main arteries in the cardiovascular system.', 'Apollo program\n10. Describe the function of the vena cava in the cardiovascular system.', 'Apollo program\n1. The main function of the heart is to pump blood throughout the body.', 'Apollo program\n2. The four chambers of the heart are the right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium, and left ventricle.', 'Apollo program\n3. The pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood from the heart to the lungs, where it picks up oxygen and releases carbon dioxide.', "Apollo program\n4. Oxygen transport in the body occurs when hemoglobin in red blood cells binds to oxygen in the lungs and then carries it to the body's tissues, where oxygen is released and carbon dioxide is picked up and transported back to the lungs for exhalation.", 'Apollo program\n5. The heart valves regulate the direction of blood flow through the heart, ensuring that blood flows in the correct direction and preventing backflow.', 'Apollo program\n6. The aorta is the largest artery in the body and carries oxygen-rich blood from the heart to the rest of the body.', 'Apollo program\n7. The two types of blood vessels are arteries, which carry oxygen-rich blood away from the heart, and veins, which carry deoxygenated blood back to the heart.', 'Apollo program\n8. The function of veins in the cardiovascular system is to transport deoxygenated blood back to the heart, ultimately returning it to the lungs where it is reoxygenated.', 'Apollo program\n9. The two main arteries in the cardiovascular system are the aorta and the pulmonary artery.', "Apollo program\n10. The vena cava is the largest vein in the body and carries deoxygenated blood from the body's tissues back to the heart for reoxygenation.", 'Apollo program\nBut even after NASA reached internal agreement, it was far from smooth sailing. Kennedy\'s science advisor Jerome Wiesner, who had expressed his opposition to manned spaceflight to Kennedy before the President took office, and had opposed the decision to land men on the Moon, hired Golovin, who had left NASA, to chair his own "Space Vehicle Panel", ostensibly to monitor, but actually to second-guess NASA\'s decisions on the Saturn V launch vehicle and LOR by forcing Shea, Seamans, and even Webb to defend themselves, delaying its formal announcement to the press on July 11, 1962, and forcing Webb to still hedge the decision as "tentative".'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Apollo program', 'context': 'But even after NASA reached internal agreement, it was far from smooth sailing. Kennedy\'s science advisor Jerome Wiesner, who had expressed his opposition to manned spaceflight to Kennedy before the President took office, and had opposed the decision to land men on the Moon, hired Golovin, who had left NASA, to chair his own "Space Vehicle Panel", ostensibly to monitor, but actually to second-guess NASA\'s decisions on the Saturn V launch vehicle and LOR by forcing Shea, Seamans, and even Webb to defend themselves, delaying its formal announcement to the press on July 11, 1962, and forcing Webb to still hedge the decision as "tentative".', 'question': "Topic: Apollo program\nWho was Kennedy's science adviser that opposed manned spacecraft flights?", 'answer': 'Jerome Wiesner'}, {'title': 'Apollo program', 'context': 'But even after NASA reached internal agreement, it was far from smooth sailing. Kennedy\'s science advisor Jerome Wiesner, who had expressed his opposition to manned spaceflight to Kennedy before the President took office, and had opposed the decision to land men on the Moon, hired Golovin, who had left NASA, to chair his own "Space Vehicle Panel", ostensibly to monitor, but actually to second-guess NASA\'s decisions on the Saturn V launch vehicle and LOR by forcing Shea, Seamans, and even Webb to defend themselves, delaying its formal announcement to the press on July 11, 1962, and forcing Webb to still hedge the decision as "tentative".', 'question': "Topic: Apollo program\nWho did Wiesner hire to monitor and second guess NASA's decisions?", 'answer': 'Golovin'}, {'title': 'Apollo program', 'context': 'But even after NASA reached internal agreement, it was far from smooth sailing. Kennedy\'s science advisor Jerome Wiesner, who had expressed his opposition to manned spaceflight to Kennedy before the President took office, and had opposed the decision to land men on the Moon, hired Golovin, who had left NASA, to chair his own "Space Vehicle Panel", ostensibly to monitor, but actually to second-guess NASA\'s decisions on the Saturn V launch vehicle and LOR by forcing Shea, Seamans, and even Webb to defend themselves, delaying its formal announcement to the press on July 11, 1962, and forcing Webb to still hedge the decision as "tentative".', 'question': 'Topic: Apollo program\nWhere did Golovin work prior to joining the "Space Vehicle Panel"?', 'answer': 'NASA'}, {'title': 'Apollo program', 'context': 'But even after NASA reached internal agreement, it was far from smooth sailing. Kennedy\'s science advisor Jerome Wiesner, who had expressed his opposition to manned spaceflight to Kennedy before the President took office, and had opposed the decision to land men on the Moon, hired Golovin, who had left NASA, to chair his own "Space Vehicle Panel", ostensibly to monitor, but actually to second-guess NASA\'s decisions on the Saturn V launch vehicle and LOR by forcing Shea, Seamans, and even Webb to defend themselves, delaying its formal announcement to the press on July 11, 1962, and forcing Webb to still hedge the decision as "tentative".', 'question': 'Topic: Apollo program\nWhen was the announcement for the LOR made after being delayed?', 'answer': 'July 11, 1962'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
