13:41:38 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Doctor Who\nTVO introduced which TV series in 1976?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 1: Doctor Who', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 2:  When TVO first started airing Doctor Who?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 2: 1976', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 3:  TVO began airing Doctor Who after watching what?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 3: The Three Doctors', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 4:  Who introduced the episode and offered educational context about the show in the 1980s?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 4: Science-fiction writer Judith Merril.', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 5:  What happened when TVO aired The Talons of Weng-Chiang?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 5: It was cancelled due to accusations of racism.', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 6:  The Talons of Weng-Chiang was aired again by what TV channel?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 6: The show was later broadcasted on cable station YTV in the 1990s.', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 7:  When did the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation begin to air Doctor Who again?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 7: 2005', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 8:  In what year did the series move to Space, a Canadian cable channel?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 8: 2009', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 9:  Where was the Doctor Who series originally aired in Canada?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 9: TVO', 'Doctor Who\nQuestion 10:  What led to the cancellation of TVO airing The Talons of Weng-Chiang?', 'Doctor Who\nAnswer 10: The show was accused of being racist.', "Doctor Who\nTVOntario picked up the show in 1976 beginning with The Three Doctors and aired each series (several years late) through to series 24 in 1991. From 1979 to 1981, TVO airings were bookended by science-fiction writer Judith Merril who would introduce the episode and then, after the episode concluded, try to place it in an educational context in keeping with TVO's status as an educational channel. Its airing of The Talons of Weng-Chiang was cancelled as a result of accusations that the story was racist; the story was later broadcast in the 1990s on cab